  "subtitle": "Pflaumenkuchen: yeasted tray bake topped with halved plums and cinnamon sugar",
  "excerpt": "German plum kuchen (Pflaumenkuchen or Zwetschgenkuchen) is a yeasted tray bake from the late summer plum season: a thin, pillowy dough base covered in rows of halved plums pressed in cut-side up, then scattered with cinnamon sugar and baked until the plums soften and the dough is golden. It is sold by the slab in German bakeries from August onward and eaten warm with whipped cream or cold the next day.",
