  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Pflaumenkuchen is one of the most widely made seasonal cakes in Germany, particularly in Baden-Württemberg and Bavaria where Italian prune plums (Zwetschgen) ripen from mid-August onward. The yeasted version predates the shorter version and is documented in German cookery books from the 19th century onward. Henriette Davidis's Praktisches Kochbuch (1845 and subsequent editions) documents a version under Pflaumenkuchen. The recipe here follows the traditional thin yeasted base format.",
