  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Plum kuchen is the most undemanding of yeasted cakes: the dough is rolled out, pressed into a tray, covered in plums, and baked. There is no enrichment beyond a little butter and egg, and no shaping skill needed. Use firm, ripe prune plums (Italian plums, Damson-type) if you can find them: they hold their shape during baking and have the right acidity to balance the sugar topping. Very ripe dessert plums collapse into the dough and make the base soggy."
          }
        ]
      },
